(RAG SYSTEMS ENGINEERING HANDBOOK) Tj T*
(Page 2: Dense vs Sparse Retrieval and Hybrid Fusion) Tj T* T*
T*
(Dense vector embeddings and sparse lexical search serve complementary retrieval goals.) Tj T*
(Dense retrieval maps text to dense semantic vectors using the BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5) Tj T*
(embedding model. It excels at semantic similarity, conceptual search, and matching) Tj T*
(synonyms, but struggles with exact alphanumeric strings like serial numbers and error codes.) Tj T*
T*
(Conversely, sparse lexical search uses the BM25 algorithm based on term frequency and) Tj T*
(inverse document frequency \(TF-IDF\). BM25 guarantees precision for exact keyword queries,) Tj T*
(technical identifiers, and uncommon acronyms.) Tj T*
T*
(The hybrid retrieval strategy combines both approaches using EnsembleRetriever with) Tj T*
(Reciprocal Rank Fusion \(RRF\). Equal weighting coefficients of 0.5 for BM25 and 0.5 for) Tj T*
(dense vector retrieval yield optimal recall across diverse query patterns.) Tj T*
(The BM25 index is built from the exact same text chunks stored in Chroma and is rebuilt) Tj T*
(whenever new documents are ingested.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
