(RAG SYSTEMS ENGINEERING HANDBOOK) Tj T*
(Page 3: Cross-Encoder Reranking and Latency Characteristics) Tj T* T*
T*
(First-stage retrieval systems prioritize high recall by scanning thousands of documents) Tj T*
(in sub-millisecond time. However, vector cosine similarity ignores cross-token interaction) Tj T*
(between the query and document passages.) Tj T*
T*
(To maximize precision, the hybrid_rerank strategy employs a two-stage retrieval pipeline.) Tj T*
(Stage one retrieves an expanded candidate pool of 15 candidate passages using hybrid search.) Tj T*
(Stage two passes these candidates through a cross-encoder model, specifically the) Tj T*
(Xenova/ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2 model executed locally via FastEmbed ONNX runtime.) Tj T*
T*
(The cross-encoder concatenates the query and passage as a single input sequence, allowing) Tj T*
(all-to-all cross-attention across tokens. This reranks passages by true relevance scores.) Tj T*
(The top 4 highest-scoring passages are forwarded to the language model.) Tj T*
(While reranking adds approximately 35 milliseconds of CPU latency, it substantially) Tj T*
(improves precision and reduces extraneous context tokens.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
