(RAG SYSTEMS ENGINEERING HANDBOOK) Tj T*
(Page 4: Corrective RAG Workflow and LangGraph Routing) Tj T* T*
T*
(Standard RAG chains blindly pass retrieved chunks to the generator even when the) Tj T*
(retriever fails. Corrective RAG \(CRAG\) introduces self-reflection and dynamic routing) Tj T*
(implemented via a LangGraph StateGraph state machine.) Tj T*
T*
(The state machine tracks: question, current_query, documents, relevant boolean, answer,) Tj T*
(rewrites counter, and an audit trail of executed steps.) Tj T*
(Execution begins at START, flowing to the retrieve node, followed by the grade_documents node.) Tj T*
(The grade_documents node makes ONE structured LLM call to assess whether the context) Tj T*
(is sufficient to answer the user inquiry.) Tj T*
T*
(Conditional routing evaluates the grading result:) Tj T*
(1. If relevant is true, control transitions immediately to the generate node.) Tj T*
(2. If relevant is false and rewrites is less than MAX_REWRITES \(default 1\), control routes) Tj T*
(to rewrite_query, which optimizes the query string and loops back to retrieve.) Tj T*
(3. If relevant is false and rewrites reaches MAX_REWRITES, control transitions to fallback.) Tj T*
(The fallback node makes ZERO LLM calls, returning an honest refusal statement that the) Tj T*
(requested information was not found, preventing hallucinations and conserving token budget.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
