(RAG SYSTEMS ENGINEERING HANDBOOK) Tj T*
(Page 5: Production Deployment, Observability, and Experiment Tracking) Tj T* T*
T*
(Production document Q&A services require robust observability and auditability.) Tj T*
(Every HTTP request to POST /ask is processed through structured logging middleware.) Tj T*
(The middleware outputs a single JSON log line containing: request_id, endpoint, mode,) Tj T*
(strategy, latency_ms, retrieved_chunks count, llm_calls count, graph steps, and HTTP status.) Tj T*
(API keys and authorization credentials are scrubbed and never recorded in logs.) Tj T*
T*
(Experimentation and evaluation metrics are systematically tracked using MLflow in ./mlruns.) Tj T*
(Key evaluation dimensions include: retrieval hit rate, keyword correctness on answerable) Tj T*
(questions, refusal rate on unanswerable questions, average latency, and average LLM calls.) Tj T*
T*
(For containerized deployment, the application runs inside Docker based on python:3.11-slim.) Tj T*
(A dedicated non-root user \(appuser\) executes the Uvicorn ASGI server on port 8000.) Tj T*
(Embedding and reranker models are downloaded at image build time to ensure the container) Tj T*
(can boot and operate reliably in air-gapped production environments.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
